00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:57.050
I will go on living even after my death.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.440
So let me get this straight.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.910
The "Pyromaniac" in custody isn't Galvez?

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:24.910
They've run ID checks on the corpses at the crash site,
 and they found one they think is Galvez.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.330
A 97%-probability match...

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.460
Who the hell did we capture, then?

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.590
I don't know.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:44.060
Respected cyberbrain engineers are looking into that, as well as how he got Fire-Starter.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:48.140
Lots of unfamiliar names on that list.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.770
Most of the competent engineers were aboard the flight that crashed along with Murasaka.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.780
I hear that almost all of those were corporate advisors.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:02.200
And connected to American intelligence, to boot.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.780
How do you know that?!

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.370
It's not something worth hiding, is it?

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:13.880
I assume the Americans planned to have them analyze Pyromaniac after the op,

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.250
right here in Japan.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.130
It was going to be a joint investigation, but yes.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.560
They were probably just political 
opportunists on corporate retainers.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.600
I doubt they could manage a decent analysis anyway.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.310
You're saying there's another way?

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.560
It'd be faster for me to look into it.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:35.270
Or you could let me analyze Hozumi...

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.730
I can't let you do either.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.490
You don't have authority.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.200
So then give it to me. And a budget.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.540
I'm ironing things out with the Prime Minister.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.870
Look through this.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:01.800
What is this?

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.630
A job for your team.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:09.600
Hozumi's being secretly transferred 
over to the Americans at 0100 hours.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.520
You're going to transport her.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.350
We're giving top secret intel to the Americans?

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:23.110
The state secrets in her cyberbrain will be returned to us, and Hozumi will ostensibly be in exile.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.380
Excuse me, ma'am, do you have an appointment?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.010
Yes. Here's my interview request form.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.940
I didn't think we'd meet like this again.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.530
Our fates must be tied.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.610
Pyromaniac just set back the schedule.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.740
Trust me, I had no intention of setting foot here again.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:15.120
Everyone who uses the Fire-Starter virus believes it will change the world.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.210
You only believe in the reality before you, 
so you wouldn't understand.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.170
Your opinion is illuminating, but we're done chatting.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:26.630
This is goodbye, ex-Colonel Hozumi.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:30.600
The Net will give me life after death.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.560
It's getting foggy!

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.070
Will we even need our optical camo?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.860
Looking at how much snow's been piling up, 
I don't think fog is going to be the main issue.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.660
Oh!

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.780
Men!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.700
Time for our field trip.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.500
She's in a bad mood.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:06:01.710
Because it's a rookie job. We already took care of most of the guys after Hozumi.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.170
Her cyberbrain's gonna be scrapped anyway. Why are we handling her with kid gloves?

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:10.640
She's being kept alive because she's still useful.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.060
As long as that remains the case, we have to treat her that way.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:18.140
An awfully delicate sentiment for someone who looks so pissed off.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.060
Got an earful from that old ape?

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.060
No.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.570
Let's load her in the truck and get moving.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.160
Major!

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.410
The job's going as planned, <i>Chief</i>.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.370
Pyromaniac just broke free.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.330
He escaped?!

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:47.340
All security in the facility has been silenced.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.010
Hold on, I'm putting my men on the line.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.180
Go on.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:58.470
He fried the brains of all the engineers there and two of the American agents.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.860
Those are all the security codes, I swear!

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.570
Let all be cast into the flames.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.190
No, don't—

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:19.750
He stole the security codes of all the engineers we convened, and now he's on the loose.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:25.710
So he let himself be captured because 
he was after those codes the whole time?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.960
What game is he playing?

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:31.680
We're working with the Americans now to track him down.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.800
You transport Hozumi as planned.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:42.600
Pyromaniac is only acting based upon the false memories Fire-Starter inseminated him with.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:46.690
If he shows up, let the Americans make the arrest.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:49.570
Avoid contact if at all possible.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.650
And if it isn't?

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.530
I authorize deadly force.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:01.660
Now that we know we can't get useful information from him, don't take unnecessary risks.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.960
Your answer?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.090
Yes, sir.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.010
You keep your promises.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.640
Are you a fellow disciple of the flame?

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:23.440
No, you're just an extension of my plans.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.270
I'm only using you.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:30.280
Fire-Starter will spark the evolution of all men's Ghosts.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.490
Therefore, it must be protected.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.320
It must use cyberbrains to mature...

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:40.080
Then be returned to the Net?

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.370
Yes.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:43.460
I'll grant you your wish.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:49.420
Then I shall fight for what I believe in.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.420
To burn everything to ash...

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:32.340
Are we gonna hand over Hozumi and call it a day, like the old ape said?

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.050
If everything goes smoothly.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:41.060
If he lost his selfhood before he
 was captured, how did he escape?

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.890
You're saying he had inside help?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.020
It's likely.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:51.900
If Pyromaniac erased the security cameras footage,
 we might as well give up hope.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.530
Anyway, our options are limited.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:59.910
Without a video trail, finding him will take good, old-fashioned legwork.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.540
Ugh, crime scene investigation?

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.450
We can let the new guy handle the scutwork.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.430
You're a real prince.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.350
What just happened?!

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.930
Missiles!

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.520
It's a UCAV.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.980
An American combat drone?!

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:37.030
I've been expecting you, Pyromaniac.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.790
Someone leaked our location.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.330
He must've gotten to the agents.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.600
Come in, Chief. It's Kusanagi.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.810
Looks like we're cut off from HQ.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.360
We can't win without attacking Pyromaniac.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.190
What now, Major?

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.770
Major, I can't get a firing angle!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.520
You three focus on shielding us!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.730
Roger!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.660
Huh? It's going home.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:10.330
No.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:14.290
He cut off our retreat and led us here.
 Don't let your guard down.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:17.250
Great, an American Army base? Can't say I'm thrilled.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.340
What?!

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:25.470
Major!

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:31.890
Shit.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.370
We're here!

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.160
That was close, huh?

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.920
Those guys were American Special Forces.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.130
With the virus controlling 'em they're no smarter than AIs,

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.380
but the optical camouflage is a problem.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.680
Yep, we're surrounded.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.850
He's obsessed. Who takes things this far?

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:19.230
They don't call you "maniac" for being sane.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:26.700
This guy'll blow up a plane just to get rid of engineers who <i>might</i> make a Fire-Starter vaccine.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:31.950
We've got the Major, who <i>did</i> make one, and Hozumi, who knows the source.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:35.120
He'd do whatever it took to kill them.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.420
This is a bad joke.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.380
Ishikawa.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.710
Find a terminal and get us a line to the Chief.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.630
Take Paz and Togusa.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:48.590
Borma, try to keep the soldiers at a distance. Saito, ditto the chopper.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:52.430
Batou, take two Logicomas and back them up.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.930
I'm the decoy now?!

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.520
What're <i>you</i> gonna do?

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.230
Take Hozumi's head and run?

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:03.820
I'll use the last Logicoma as a booster and seize Pyromaniac's Net.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.690
Can you do that with just one?

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.570
I'll use my personal Net.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:08.700
Personal?

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:13.290
I run hacking tests whenever I build a security system.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.870
I have a network made up of the debuggers I use.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:21.210
Section 9's security codes have probably been overwritten.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.960
I might have some trouble reconnecting.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.420
Work as fast as you can.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.970
We'll need the Chief's backroom dealing if this turns into open battle.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.180
Let's go!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.470
Okay!

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.230
What if they storm you during your dive?!

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.480
We can't protect you from out there!

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.440
You have command if they do!

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:47.690
Don't die.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.120
Logicomas!

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.540
Okay!

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:07.800
Wow, is this your personal Net, Major?

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.010
Yes.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:12.260
The Nets run by corporate admins don't even compare.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:15.430
This is a battlefield populated by distrustful savages.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:23.560
Anyone want to join a game of mine?

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.360
Want to join?!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.090
They took the bait.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:01.390
Are you getting the hackers to eradicate the virus?

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:05.940
Of course not. They're only breaking through the soldiers' barriers to disable them.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.400
Huh? But the Army uses <i>attack</i> barriers!

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:12.610
So? Focus on your own work.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.780
Someone is trying to crack you from outside.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:18.290
He's here.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.370
You maintain these connections.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.540
Roger!

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:33.130
Phony cyberbrain space?

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.840
Looks like a Kuzan battlefield...

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:45.480
<i>I still don't sense a Ghost. So the virus itself is running him?</i>

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:50.690
Is this what you saw—or rather, Galvez's memory?

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.950
Who are you?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:58.910
I am Galvez, and Emma, and Murasaka.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.950
All Ghosts are me.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:04.290
An aggregate of the false memories, then.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.630
That's not what we call a "Ghost."

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.090
You're nothing but a vessel created by the virus.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.550
Looks like the Major's doing well.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:22.100
Okay.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:34.610
Did he get it?

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.370
Shit!

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:51.500
I have received a revelation from Fire-Starter.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.050
That is my everything.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:59.930
I must burn all threats to Fire-Starter.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:03.310
So your goal is to eliminate all possibility of erasing the virus.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:07.890
Ultimately, you're another puppet of the virus.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:12.940
If your personality is nothing but false memories it molded,

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.440
further conversation is meaningless.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:18.360
Major, should we take control?

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:21.530
Our chances of bulldozing him aren't good. Leave him to me.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:25.660
Fire-Starter will spark the evolution of all men's Ghosts.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:31.630
Your cyberbrain will be used to bring out its potential.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.510
I'm out of ammo!

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.600
Shit!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.480
We're back online!

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:50.780
What is it?

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:53.360
This is Ishikawa, Chief. That Pyromaniac guy—

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.320
This is bad...

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.200
Uh-oh!

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:12.210
Major!

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.250
Major, time to withdraw!

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.460
She's still in her dive!

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.890
Dammit! I'm draggin' you with me!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:25.350
You are the greatest sinner here.

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:39.990
Link with me, and go on living even after your death.

00:19:47.810 --> 00:19:52.330
Sorry, but I'm not that pessimistic about the real world.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:56.290
And I'm not quite yet old enough to worry about the afterlife.

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:59.590
It's over, Pyromaniac. Disappear.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.770
Good work.

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:27.830
What the...

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:29.950
Major!

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:32.410
Batou, is this your doing?

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:33.960
You took care of things?

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:34.710
Yes.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.710
What happened to Pyromaniac?

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:40.170
He's extinct.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:58.160
Pyromaniac's cyberbrain held nothing but memories related to the hit on Hozumi

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:02.280
and a few deeply implanted lines from <i>The Fiery Angel</i>.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:08.610
This whole mess will be tied up in secret, after some fairly involved negotiations.

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:12.080
I told you, you should've let me handle it.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:13.620
Lay off.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:19.210
Just be grateful you're not getting punished for trashing an American base.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:24.050
I'll have their agents stay out of the Pyromaniac affair for now, too.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:29.100
They knew about the Flight 381 
bombing in advance, didn't they?

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:34.980
Fire-Starter switched hosts because the Americans crowded Galvez.

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:39.740
They knew it was going to take Murasaka and the engineers down with Galvez,

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:44.070
but they waited until Pyromaniac had security codes from around the globe.

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:45.780
Where did you hear that?

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:48.200
Did you think I'd come back from a dive empty-handed?

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:53.080
I found an agent's memories in
 Pyromaniac's auxiliary cyberbrain.

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:56.370
I'll do you a favor and pretend I didn't hear that.

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:57.750
Keep it to yourself.

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:02.680
Put on a uniform.

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:05.970
We'll meet at the Prime Minister's residence at 0900 hours.

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:16.140
He wants to personally thank your squad 
for nabbing the terrorist behind Flight 381.

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:23.530
We've finished refining the virus.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:28.740
Not much longer now...

00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:40.670
You must be Kusanagi.

00:22:42.770 --> 00:22:44.170
I hear you've done us a great service.

00:22:46.180 --> 00:22:47.720
